  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $A$ to $C$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AC}=\\overset{\\to }{AF}+\\overset{\\to }{FE}+\\overset{\\to }{EG}+\\overset{\\to }{GC}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/e24ac0b6cf4f039cd1e8b2e1aa5dd921ea637fb2fe46666a0091372dfce87d44.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AF}=c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{FE}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{EG}=-b\\,\\overset{\\to }{GC}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/37c3758dc7a4c8a5b79c3e687e77f62090282410e3bf45bfade3494cd3b8055b.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} & =\\overset{\\to }{AF}+\\overset{\\to }{FE}+\\overset{\\to }{EG}+\\overset{\\to }{GC} \\\\  & =c+(-a)+(-b)+d \\\\  & =c-a-b+d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
